I wrote the conclusion to `.governor/conclusions/ledgerkit-spec-orientation.md`. You can load it into a later session with `/merge ledgerkit-spec-orientation`.

It covers:
- how the three exports differ on dates and amounts;
- the traps I found in the existing code;
- your two changes to `report` (semicolons, refunds counted by default);
- your house rules;
- five open questions.

Before writing it I re-checked the key facts against the code and they all held. The A reader still fails on the sample, code 5200 is "Contract Labor", `normalize()` drops refunds by default, B's `110003` converts to $1,100.03, and C's `13/03/2026` only parses day first. The 6 existing tests still pass, so nothing in the file is marked unverified.

The story questions from this session are left out because they have nothing to do with ledgerkit.
